WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:18.450
The second term at Redmond sped by as quickly as the first, and Anne enjoyed it thoroughly.

2
00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:22.802
She studied hard, for she wanted to win a scholarship in English.

3
00:00:22.803 --> 00:00:31.643
If she won it, the scholarship would pay for her tuition fees at Redmond College next year, and she would not have to use Marilla's savings.

4
00:00:31.644 --> 00:00:39.186
Gilbert, too, was hoping to get a scholarship, but he still found plenty of time to drop in and visit Anne at her boardinghouse.

5
00:00:39.187 --> 00:00:45.635
He was Anne's escort to most college events, and Anne knew students gossiped about them being a "couple."

6
00:00:45.636 --> 00:00:50.937
The gossip made Anne furious, but she could not refuse Gilbert's company.

7
00:00:50.938 --> 00:00:57.631
He was her old friend, and she would feel bad declining his kind offers to accompany her to college events.

8
00:00:57.632 --> 00:01:01.279
Besides, he had stopped acting like a suitor toward her.

9
00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:06.684
Anne was very glad of that, though she did secretly wonder why he'd changed.

10
00:01:06.685 --> 00:01:10.827
Only one disagreeable incident spoiled that winter.

11
00:01:10.828 --> 00:01:17.277
One night Charlie Sloane asked Anne if she would promise "to become Mrs. Charlie Sloane some day."

12
00:01:17.278 --> 00:01:21.162
Of course, Anne knew that she could never marry Charlie.

13
00:01:21.163 --> 00:01:25.161
After all, he was not her romantic hero either!

14
00:01:25.162 --> 00:01:33.824
"Another unromantic proposal!" Anne sighed. "Where is my Prince Charming?"

15
00:01:33.825 --> 00:01:38.076
The next day Anne scurried into Priscilla's room.

16
00:01:38.077 --> 00:01:46.146
"Read that," she cried, tossing Priscilla a letter from Stella Maynard, who had been one of their friends at Queen's College.

17
00:01:46.147 --> 00:01:49.801
"Stella is coming to Redmond to study next year.

18
00:01:49.802 --> 00:01:55.986
Tell me what you think of her idea. I think it's wonderful, if it's possible."

19
00:01:55.987 --> 00:01:59.882
"Anne, I have a little plan," Stella had written.

20
00:01:59.883 --> 00:02:06.201
"You know how I hate boarding. I've boarded for four years and I'm so sick of it.

21
00:02:06.202 --> 00:02:10.230
I can imagine you are not a huge fan of boardinghouses either.

22
00:02:10.231 --> 00:02:15.955
Why don't you and Priscilla and I rent a little house somewhere in Halifax?"

23
00:02:15.956 --> 00:02:20.692
"I think it's a good idea," said Priscilla after she read the letter.

24
00:02:20.693 --> 00:02:28.784
"So do I," agreed Anne delightedly. "Let's go house-hunting at once, before exams start."

25
00:02:28.785 --> 00:02:33.873
"I'm afraid it will be hard to get a house that fits our budget," warned Priscilla.

26
00:02:33.874 --> 00:02:37.439
"We'll have to be happy with a shabby little place."

27
00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:46.233
Over the next few days, they saw many houses, but they were either too big, too small, too expensive, or too far from Redmond.

28
00:02:46.234 --> 00:02:50.495
The house-hunting was not going well.

29
00:02:50.496 --> 00:02:59.437
A few weeks later, Anne and Priscilla were walking home the usual way, down Spofford Avenue, so that they could look at Patty's Place.

30
00:02:59.438 --> 00:03:07.444
As they stopped to admire the garden, Anne suddenly shouted, "Look, look! Am I seeing things, Priscilla?

31
00:03:07.445 --> 00:03:14.152
Look over there and tell me if it's true!" Priscilla looked where Anne was pointing.

32
00:03:14.153 --> 00:03:18.396
Over the arched gateway of Patty's Place dangled a little sign.

33
00:03:18.397 --> 00:03:23.726
It said "For Rent. Furnished. Inquire Within."

34
00:03:23.727 --> 00:03:30.399
"Priscilla," said Anne in a whisper, "is it possible we could rent Patty's Place?"

35
00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:40.443
"It's too good to be true, Anne. Fairy tales don't happen nowadays . . . But then again maybe they do," Priscilla replied excitedly.

36
00:03:40.444 --> 00:03:46.371
"Anyway, it's too late to knock on their door this evening. Let's come back tomorrow."

37
00:03:46.372 --> 00:03:50.372
Early the next evening, the girls went back to Patty's Place.

38
00:03:50.373 --> 00:03:55.423
They knocked on the door rather timidly, and then stepped into a large living room.

39
00:03:55.424 --> 00:03:58.385
Two old ladies sat by the fire.

40
00:03:58.386 --> 00:04:04.959
They were very similar, except that one looked about seventy years old and the other fifty.

41
00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:10.091
They were both knitting, and the older one invited Anne and Priscilla to take a seat.

42
00:04:10.092 --> 00:04:17.372
Behind each lady sat a large white china dog, with a green nose and ears and green spots all over.

43
00:04:17.373 --> 00:04:23.088
Anne liked the dogs straight away; they seemed to her like the guardians of Patty's Place.

44
00:04:23.089 --> 00:04:33.018
For a few minutes nobody spoke. The girls were too nervous, and the ladies were content to knit and wait for their guests to speak first.

45
00:04:33.019 --> 00:04:37.753
Anne glanced about the room. What a nice place it was!

46
00:04:37.754 --> 00:04:47.033
Finally she spoke. "We . . . we . . . saw your sign that this house is for rent," said Anne to the older lady.

47
00:04:47.034 --> 00:04:54.156
"Oh, yes," said Miss Patty. "I meant to take that sign down today."

48
00:04:54.157 --> 00:04:59.721
"Oh, are we too late?" asked Anne, barely hiding her disappointment.

49
00:04:59.722 --> 00:05:06.804
"No," Miss Patty said. "We have decided not to rent it after all."

50
00:05:06.805 --> 00:05:12.423
"What a shame!" exclaimed Anne. "I love this place so much.

51
00:05:12.424 --> 00:05:15.344
I really hoped we could have lived here."

52
00:05:15.345 --> 00:05:18.453
"You love it?" said Miss Patty.

53
00:05:18.454 --> 00:05:26.761
"I really do love it," Anne said. "I've loved it ever since I first saw it last fall."

54
00:05:26.762 --> 00:05:30.251
"You're not just saying that you 'love it'?

55
00:05:30.252 --> 00:05:35.409
Young people 'love' everything these days," said Miss Patty.

56
00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:42.566
"No, I really adore this house. Priscilla and I walk by it often," Anne said.

57
00:05:42.567 --> 00:05:47.173
"If you love it, you can have it," said Miss Patty.

58
00:05:47.174 --> 00:05:54.685
"I decided today that I wouldn't rent it because we didn't like any of the people who asked to rent it.

59
00:05:54.686 --> 00:06:01.225
You are different. I believe you do love it and will take care of it."

60
00:06:01.226 --> 00:06:04.407
"If . . . if we can afford the rent.

61
00:06:04.408 --> 00:06:08.364
We have a limited budget," said Anne meekly.

62
00:06:08.365 --> 00:06:15.442
Miss Patty named the amount. Anne and Priscilla looked at each other, and Priscilla shook her head.

63
00:06:15.443 --> 00:06:24.543
"I'm afraid we can't afford it," said Anne, choking back her disappointment. "We're only students and we're poor."

64
00:06:24.544 --> 00:06:31.719
"What can you afford?" asked Miss Patty. Anne named her amount and Miss Patty nodded.

65
00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:34.788
"That will do. You can move in.

66
00:06:34.789 --> 00:06:38.920
We leave in two months, at the start of next term.

67
00:06:38.921 --> 00:06:44.010
You don't object, I hope, to this house being called Patty's Place?"

68
00:06:44.011 --> 00:06:49.129
"No, that's one of the nicest things about it," Anne said, smiling.

69
00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:59.653
Patty's Place was theirs. At least one small dream had come true!
